From: "Christopher L. Weeks" <C576653@MIZZOU1.missouri.edu>
Subject: Mongrelization of America's Intelligence

About five years ago I read a study on the decrease of American intelligence.
(Sorry I have no reference to give) At the time, it seemed form the description
of the experimental proceedure given, that the study was as fair as could be
reasonably assumed.  The gist of the study was that the bell curve of IQ tests
done on American first through twelfth grade students had flattened out and
extended both left and right over a period of 30(ish?) years.  The researchers
decided that the average person had significantly lower IQ scores while the
extension to the extremes was almost wholly caused by increase in technology
and population.  One interesting note made by the authors was that the curve's
extension toward the lower scores was more rapid than the extension toward the
higher scores.  Apparently our ability to keep people alive who have lower
quality mental faculties is increasing more rapidly than our natal care systems
which are designed to increase the health and intelligence of the baby.

Has anybody else read this?  If so please let me know where it was published.
It was in a professional journal of education or psychology as I recall.



